 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to accessibility to bone\nmarrow registry information; and to amend a chapter of the laws of 2020,\namending the public health law relating to requiring the department of health\nto develop and disseminate information regarding bone marrow donor programs\nand authorizing physicians, physician assistants and nurse practitioners to\nprovide such information to patients, as proposed in legislative bills numbers\nS. 6705 and A. 5370-A, in relation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S865",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S865-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §4369, Pub Health L; amd §2, Chap of 2020 (as proposed in S.6705 & A.5370-A)",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S865\n\nSPONSOR: BENJAMIN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to accessibility to\nbone marrow registry information; and to amend a chapter of the laws of\n2020, amending the public health law relating to requiring the depart-\nment of health to develop and disseminate information regarding bone\nmarrow donor programs and authorizing physicians, physician assistants\nand nurse practitioners to provide such information to patients, as\nproposed in legislative bills numbers S. 6705 and A. 5370-A, in relation\nto the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2020,\nch. 287.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by removing the require-\nment that the information on bone marrow registries be distributed to\nall primary healthcare providers and instead requires the information to\nbe made accessible on DOH's website for providers to give to their\npatients. In addition, the effective date of the underlying chapter is\nchanged from January 1 to one year after the effective date of the bill.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPursuant to approval memo 15 of 2020, the Executive expressed concern\nthat there was not ample time for DOH to develop these materials and\nthat the language of the underlying chapter may have caused confusion as\nto whether patients must receive this information. This legislation is a\nnegotiated change to the underlying chapter that addresses those\nconcerns.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 287 of the Laws of 2020.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
